.TH MARBOR\-BACKUP 1 "2026-08-17" "marbor dev" "Marbor Manual"
.SH NAME
marbor\-backup \- manage marbor.db backups (P\-A2-07)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B marbor backup
[action] [args] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
manage marbor.db backups (P\-A2-07)
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B now
trigger an on\-demand backup and download it
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-output string
local file path to save to (default: server\-suggested filename)
.RE
.TP
.B list
list backup files on the server
.TP
.B restore <filename>
restore marbor.db from a backup file (marbor restarts)
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-yes
confirm restore without prompting
.RE
.TP
.B upload
upload a local .db file as a restorable backup
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-file string
local .db file path (required) (required)
.RE
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MARBOR_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MARBOR_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MARBOR_PASSWORD)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmarbor\fR(1)
